From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:00:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Enable the PCH port hotplug whatever its
 value

gma_setup_panel() enables the hotplug detection of DDI B, C and D
(PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG, from gpu_dp_*_hotplug of the devicetree) only if the
register reads 0, and leaves it as it is otherwise. At boot, and on S3
resume with gfx_resume_init on, libgfxinit enables the detection of the
ports itself right after; with the display left to the OS at wake,
nothing else touches the register before the OS. The live HPD state of
a port in SDEISR follows its pin only with the detection of the port
enabled, and macOS (AppleIntelFramebufferAzul) reads that of the panel
port at wake, before it turns the panel on: if it is low, the display
stays off.

Program the fields of the three ports whatever the register holds, as
libgfxinit and Linux do, without writing the status bits back as 1:
they are write-1-to-clear, and what they latched is for the OS. Log the
register before and after, and, on the resume path that leaves the
display to the OS, SDEISR and PP_STATUS: the HPD state that the OS will
find there, and whether the panel has power. An eDP panel raises its
HPD only once powered on (T3), and this path does not power it on.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. On the
host, the expression with the devicetree of the W541 (4, 4, 4) writes
0x00101010 over 0, and over any other value sets the three fields, keeps
the other bits and writes the status bits as 0.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c
index a3e5b04ce8..578d5a4d3e 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/gma.c
@@ -72,6 +72,11 @@ u32 map_oprom_vendev(u32 vendev)
 	return new_vendev;
 }
 
+/* PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG: the enable and pulse duration fields of DDI B, C and D */
+#define PCH_HOTPLUG_PORTS_MASK		(0x7 << 18 | 0x7 << 10 | 0x7 << 2)
+/* PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG: the status bits of the ports, write-1-to-clear */
+#define PCH_HOTPLUG_STATUS_MASK		0x03030303
+
 static struct resource *gtt_res = NULL;
 
 u32 gtt_read(u32 reg)
@@ -320,13 +325,21 @@ static void gma_setup_panel(struct device *dev)
 	const struct i915_gpu_panel_config *panel_cfg = &conf->panel_cfg;
 	u32 reg32;
 
-	/* Setup Digital Port Hotplug */
-	reg32 = gtt_read(PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG);
-	if (!reg32) {
-		reg32 = (conf->gpu_dp_b_hotplug & 0x7) << 2;
-		reg32 |= (conf->gpu_dp_c_hotplug & 0x7) << 10;
-		reg32 |= (conf->gpu_dp_d_hotplug & 0x7) << 18;
+	/*
+	 * Setup Digital Port Hotplug, whatever the register holds: the live HPD
+	 * state of a port in SDEISR follows its pin only with the detection of
+	 * the port enabled, and when the display is left to the OS at wake,
+	 * nothing else enables it before the OS looks. The status bits are
+	 * write-1-to-clear: write them as 0, and leave them to the OS.
+	 */
+	const u32 hotplug = (conf->gpu_dp_b_hotplug & 0x7) << 2 |
+			    (conf->gpu_dp_c_hotplug & 0x7) << 10 |
+			    (conf->gpu_dp_d_hotplug & 0x7) << 18;
+	if (hotplug) {
+		const u32 old = gtt_read(PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG);
+		reg32 = (old & ~(PCH_HOTPLUG_PORTS_MASK | PCH_HOTPLUG_STATUS_MASK)) | hotplug;
 		gtt_write(PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG, reg32);
+		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "GMA: PCH_PORT_HOTPLUG %08x -> %08x\n", old, reg32);
 	}
 
 	/* Setup Panel Power On Delays */
@@ -690,6 +703,9 @@ static void gma_func0_init(struct device *dev)
 			       "IGD is not decoding legacy VGA MEM and IO: skipping NATIVE graphic init\n");
 		} else if (display_to_os) {
 			printk(BIOS_INFO, "S3 resume: display left to the OS\n");
+			/* What the OS finds: the live HPD state, the panel power */
+			printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "GMA: SDEISR %08x, PP_STATUS %08x\n",
+			       gtt_read(SDEISR), gtt_read(PCH_PP_STATUS));
 		} else {
 			printk(BIOS_SPEW, "NATIVE graphics, run native enable\n");
 			gma_gfxinit(&lightup_ok);
-- 
